# OMMigrate .gitignore
# Keeps runtime data, test data, and OS noise out of the repository.
# The repo contains only source code and documentation.
# All runtime output lives in Documents\OutlookMigration\ on the operator's machine.

# ── Runtime data folders ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are created at Documents\OutlookMigration\ by the scripts.
# They should never appear in the repo.
Config/
Logs/
Manifests/
Reports/
Backups/

# ── Outlook data files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.pst
*.ost
*.nst

# ── OMMigrate generated output files ─────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*_Audit.log
*_Complete.json
*_Checkpoint.json
*_Settings.json
migration_accounts.csv
folder_map.csv
rules_inventory.csv
Discovery_Report_*.html
Backup_Report_*.html
Migration_Report_*.html
Rollback_Report_*.html
RECOVERY.txt

# ── Windows OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# ── PowerShell artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.pssproj
*.psproj

# ── Editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.vs/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
*.bak
*~

# ── Obsidian noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# workspace.json/workspace-mobile.json record per-session UI state (open tabs,
# pane layout, scroll position) and change every time a .md file is viewed in
# Obsidian -- not project data, no value to anyone else cloning the repo.
# app.json/appearance.json are per-user app preferences (theme, font, CSS
# snippets, general app settings) -- an operator who installs the Obsidian
# Add-on and customizes their view should never have those personal
# preferences silently overwritten by a future repo update, nor show as
# permanent uncommitted changes. Administrator's explicit direction (2026-08-18):
# don't let a tracked file capture something a user customizes locally.
# community-plugins.json/core-plugins.json are intentionally left tracked --
# they define which plugins/features are enabled at all (e.g. html-viewer-
# plus, bundled specifically so the donate button renders), not a per-user
# cosmetic preference within an already-enabled feature.
# The rest of .obsidian/ (the bundled vault config, HTML Viewer Plus plugin,
# etc.) IS intentionally tracked -- see Install.ps1's FilesToDownload list.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/graph.json
.obsidian/app.json
.obsidian/appearance.json

# ── Temp files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.tmp
*.temp

# ── Git placeholders no longer needed ────────────────────────────────────────
.gitkeep
